00\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A SPECIAL MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 17, 2007\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. in Conference Room No. 2, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Tamuri.\r\rCLOSED SESSION\r\rThe City Council recessed at 7:01 p.m. into closed session to confer with legal counsel regarding the following:\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015One matter of Anticipated Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(b)(3)(A), facts and circumstances that might result in litigation but which the City believes are not yet known to potential plaintiff or plaintiffs.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015One matter of Initiation of Litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54956.9(c).\r\rPending litigation, pursuant to Government Code Section 54946.9(a): Smith v. City of Calabasas, BS106644; Cooper v. Calabasas Park Estates Owners Association,�BC323695; Toby Keeler and Elizabeth Stephens v. City of Calabasas, BS109503.\r\rThe City Council reconvened at 7:25 p.m. from closed session, and Mayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Peirce, Steller, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Terilyn Finders.\r\rMichael G. Colantuono, City Attorney, stated that the Council did not take any action in closed session which required reporting. Mayor Bozajian stated that the closed session will continue upon the adjournment of the regular meeting.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rTerilyn Finders, President of the Las Virgenes Unified School District Board of Education, introduced three principals who have recently undertaken new school assignments in Calabasas: Karen Hanson at Bay Laurel Elementary School, Summer Harding at Chaparral Elementary School and Sheila Grady at Lupin Hill Elementary School. Mayor Bozajian presented proclamations to members of the organization, Teens Against Domestic Violence. Mayor pro Tem Maurer announced that October is �National Domestic Violence Awareness Month.� Councilmember Washburn spoke regarding the upcoming Calabasas Pumpkin Festival that will be taking place on Saturday and Sunday, October 22 � 23, 2007. Mayor Bozajian spoke regarding the City�s recent participation in Agoura Hill�s Reyes Adobe Days Parade and the Tennis Tournament that will be occurring at the Calabasas Tennis & Swim Center. He also spoke regarding the upcoming Election on November 6, 2007 and encouraged everyone to vote.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\rAlan Saxe, Measure E Oversight Committee, provided an update on the spending for Measure E in the Las Virgenes Unified School District. Darren Proett, Calabasas, spoke in support of the City Council considering a rent stabilization ordinance.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS\r\r Approval of the minutes for the October 3, 2007 City Council meeting.\r\r Authorization to extend the expiration date for the existing professional services agreement with Newbury Park Tree Service, Inc. for general tree work on City property and public streets.\r\r Approval of sewer system management plan (SSMP) development schedule.\r\r Recommendation to approve the appointment of Sharon Boucher by Mayor pro Tem Maurer to the Public Safety Commission.\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Item #1, 2, 3 and 4. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rSPECIAL ITEM\r\r Report from Debbie Bruschaber from the MRT regarding the Dry Canyon Creek restoration project and report from Alex Farassati regarding the Las Virgenes Creek restoration project.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2007-238, amending the Municipal Code, Title 5 Business Licenses and Regulations, Chapter 5.04 Motion Picture and Television Filming Permits; and adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1101, establishing film permit fees, adopting a schedule of fees and rescinding Resolution No. 2003-825.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rDeborah Steller, Media Operations Director, presented the staff report. \r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Maurer, to introduce Ordinance No. 2007-238, an amendment to Chapter 5.04; and to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1101, establishing film permit fees, adopting a schedule of fees and rescinding Resolution No. 2003-825. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2007-240, adopting by reference, pursuant to Government Code Section 50022.2, the 2007 California Code of Regulations, Title 24 - The 2007 California Building Standards Code.\r\rMayor Bozajian opened the public hearing.\r\rSparky Cohen, Building Official, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Bozajian closed the public hearing.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to introduce Ordinance No. 2007-240, adopting by reference, the 2007 California Code of Regulations, Title 24 � The 2007 California Building Standards Code. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\r Recommendation from the Communications and Technology Commission regarding the proposed 818 area code change.\r\rDeborah Steller, Media Operations Director, and Robert Lia and Candice Weber, Communication & Technology Commissioners, presented the staff report.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to extend support for not changing the 818 area code; however, if there must be a change, the City will support a split if Calabasas retains the 818 area code. If Calabasas will not retain the 818 area code, the City will support an overlay. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Recommendation from the Public Safety Commission on the roles and responsibilities of CERP as they relate to public safety and emergency preparedness.\r\rDr. Gary Lysik, Chief Financial Officer, presented the staff report.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve the recommendations from the Public Safety Commission on the roles and responsibilities of CERP. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r Discussion regarding a Sister City visit in Summer 2008.\r\rThe City Council concurred to approve that a delegation of City Councilmembers, residents and staff may go to Anqing and Bejing, China in Summer 2008 at their own expense.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of September 27, 2007 to October 4, 2007.\r\r There was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r There were no task force reports.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r There were no future agenda items.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:40 p.m. into closed session and adjourned at 10:55 p.m. from closed session. There was no reportable action. \r\r\r\r\r_________________________________\rRobin Parker, City Clerk\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u0014- 3 -\u0015\r10/17/07\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000